# CoW Track 1A — bare `for x in coll` over a RESOURCE element materializes (gap A2).
#
# Pins gap A2: a bare-for over a RESOURCE struct element wrongly WROTE THROUGH on
# Rust gg (`x.field = v` reached the collection → `101`). §3.1 makes the bare
# element immutable, so the write must land in a private materialized copy and
# the collection stays `1`. The self-host was already correct here; 1A brings
# Rust gg into line. A read-only scan of the same element pays no clone (the
# CollectionElement borrow only materializes on the write).
# Output must be correct on BOTH backends.

struct Rec:
    String name
    int v

void main():
    Vector[Rec] a = [Rec("a", 1)]
    for x in a:
        x.v = x.v + 100
    print(a.get(0).unwrap().v)
